==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael update <path> [changes] [options]
       raphael update --id <id> [changes] [options]

Change an item with revision protection.

Give at least one change. Tags replace the complete tag list; --no-tags clears
it. A renamed title does not change the path.

A body replacement requires the revision you read. Other changes may read and
pin the current id and revision for you. Conflicts are never retried
automatically.

Rules:
  Metadata is set once, at create. --active and --inactive apply only to
    projects.
  On a revision conflict, get the item again and reconcile your intended change
    before updating with its new revision.
  A value that starts with -, such as a Markdown list, must be joined to its
    flag with =, as in `--body='- first item'`; otherwise it is read as another
    option and refused. A longer body is easier as a file or a pipe:
    `--body @list.md` or `--body @-`.

Options:
      --id <id>
          Address by stable id instead of path.
      --title <text>
          Name, at most 200 characters.
      --description <text>
          Description, at most 4000 characters. An empty string clears it.
      --slug <slug>
          Address within the parent, at most 100 characters. See
          `raphael help addressing`.
      --body <text|@file|@->
          Body text, @file, or @- for stdin. An empty string clears it. Requires
          --revision.
      --body-literal <text>
          Literal body text, including text beginning with @. Requires
          --revision.
      --body-format <format>
          Submitted body: markdown or tiptap. Default: markdown.
      --strict
          Refuse a Markdown body with constructs Raphael cannot store as
          written. See `raphael help content`.
      --tag <tag>
          Repeat for each tag; at most 25 tags of 50 characters. Commas are
          refused. Replaces all tags. Repeatable.
      --no-tags
          Clear all tags.
      --active
          Mark the project active.
      --inactive
          Mark the project inactive.
      --revision <n>
          Revision read previously. Required to replace the body; for other
          changes, an omitted revision is read just before sending.
      --return-format <format>
          Returned body: markdown or tiptap. Requires --json. Default: markdown.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael update /work/raphael/api-design --body '# Revised design' --revision 8
  raphael update /work/raphael --tag reviewed --tag contracts
  raphael update --id 42 --title 'Contract review' --description ''

Prints:
  The item with its path and revision, and the path it had when --slug changed
  it. When every value given matches what is stored it reads Unchanged and the
  revision is kept. JSON carries `entity`, `changed` and `previousPath`.

Next: raphael get --id 42

See also: raphael help revisions; raphael help content
